01:15:44.540 --> 01:15:46.860
And she asked to question number two,

01:15:46.860 --> 01:15:49.690
how do you interpret the
Pauli exclusion principle

01:15:49.690 --> 01:15:51.840
as a causal constraint?

01:15:51.840 --> 01:15:54.280
Can two electrons never actually be

01:15:54.280 --> 01:15:56.830
in the same state ontologically?

01:15:56.830 --> 01:15:58.460
For me, I would be cautious

01:15:58.460 --> 01:16:01.630
and say that this should only
be interpreted epistemically

01:16:01.630 --> 01:16:04.960
because we can never prove
this exclusion principle.

01:16:04.960 --> 01:16:06.590
So should we treat possible

01:16:06.590 --> 01:16:09.733
and impossible constraints
in different ways?

01:16:12.250 --> 01:16:13.970
- Thank you very much for this question.

01:16:13.970 --> 01:16:15.862
I suppose it's to me.

01:16:15.862 --> 01:16:18.180
- Yeah.

01:16:18.180 --> 01:16:19.840
- Okay, so Pauli's principle

01:16:19.840 --> 01:16:21.770
is really an interesting principle

01:16:21.770 --> 01:16:24.370
because in its mature formulation,

01:16:24.370 --> 01:16:26.390
it's just a mathematical principle.

01:16:26.390 --> 01:16:29.350
The wave function of this combination

01:16:29.350 --> 01:16:30.920
is to be anti symmetric

01:16:30.920 --> 01:16:33.060
and from that everything else follows

01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:34.873
about fermions in general.

01:16:36.070 --> 01:16:39.800
And I had a big argument with
a very dear colleague of mine

01:16:39.800 --> 01:16:44.783
who died at the beginning of
the pandemic of COVID virus.

01:16:47.110 --> 01:16:52.110
And he said, Pauli's
principle is a demonstration

01:16:52.570 --> 01:16:55.570
that purely mathematical principles

01:16:55.570 --> 01:16:58.440
do work for us in physics.

01:16:58.440 --> 01:17:02.980
But I looked a little more into
the history of the principle

01:17:02.980 --> 01:17:04.160
and its applications.

01:17:04.160 --> 01:17:05.170
Not so much the history,

01:17:05.170 --> 01:17:06.950
but the application of the principle.

01:17:06.950 --> 01:17:09.100
So there was a very nice application

01:17:09.100 --> 01:17:12.200
of the principle early on in 31, 32,

01:17:12.200 --> 01:17:14.300
I don't remember exactly, by Chandra Sikka

01:17:17.443 --> 01:17:22.210
who calculated the mass of a white dwarf,

01:17:22.210 --> 01:17:25.370
the limited mass beyond
which it would collapse

01:17:25.370 --> 01:17:26.933
under its own gravity.

01:17:29.010 --> 01:17:32.820
And so there is gravity pulling inside

01:17:32.820 --> 01:17:35.810
and what is a force that pulls outside

01:17:35.810 --> 01:17:40.163
and it's really the result of
Pauli's exclusion principle.

01:17:41.330 --> 01:17:43.100
And only when gravity

01:17:43.100 --> 01:17:48.100
overcomes that pressure
towards the periphery,

01:17:51.120 --> 01:17:54.180
when gravity overcomes it
and pulls the mass back,

01:17:54.180 --> 01:17:57.270
then we have the collapse.

01:17:57.270 --> 01:17:58.750
And the limited reach,

01:17:58.750 --> 01:18:02.590
which I think is around
1.4 of the mass of the sun

01:18:02.590 --> 01:18:06.057
is still very much a pre-op
if it's still accepted.

01:18:06.057 --> 01:18:07.250
- Not very much there,

01:18:07.250 --> 01:18:10.810
I mean and (indistinct)
pressure is a real thing

01:18:10.810 --> 01:18:12.470
and also you know in the laboratory

01:18:12.470 --> 01:18:15.940
when they make both Einstein condensates,

01:18:15.940 --> 01:18:17.470
they're taking advantage

01:18:17.470 --> 01:18:20.330
of the degeneracy pressure that you get.

01:18:20.330 --> 01:18:23.230
So these new states of matter and stuff.

01:18:23.230 --> 01:18:25.240
- Okay, so in that sense here

01:18:25.240 --> 01:18:26.900
it works like a causal principle

01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:29.250
because it's something
that balances gravity.

01:18:29.250 --> 01:18:32.360
So gravity, again, is very abstract

01:18:32.360 --> 01:18:34.490
and Pauli's principle is very abstract,

01:18:34.490 --> 01:18:37.700
but the applications of these principles

01:18:37.700 --> 01:18:40.260
are applications to very concrete things.

01:18:40.260 --> 01:18:42.470
And then later, many years later

01:18:42.470 --> 01:18:45.110
then when they prove the
mature form of the theory

01:18:45.110 --> 01:18:46.350
and they had to prove it,

01:18:46.350 --> 01:18:49.230
they used what they call micro causality.

01:18:49.230 --> 01:18:52.310
That is relativistic, special
relativistic principle

01:18:52.310 --> 01:18:56.920
that parallel or
analogous to no signaling.

01:18:56.920 --> 01:18:59.010
So, again, a causal principle

01:18:59.010 --> 01:19:01.140
went into the proof of the theory.

01:19:01.140 --> 01:19:04.560
So even if electrons for us

01:19:04.560 --> 01:19:07.120
and other fermions certainly
don't have an identity

01:19:07.120 --> 01:19:12.120
and we cannot track them and
find them in a certain place

01:19:12.740 --> 01:19:15.950
and say the other one
cannot get into this place.

01:19:15.950 --> 01:19:18.998
The way that principle
works and is applied

01:19:18.998 --> 01:19:20.730
is I think in harmony

01:19:20.730 --> 01:19:24.770
with I considering it a
causal principle assymetry

01:19:24.770 --> 01:19:27.443
and anti symmetry to causal constraint.

01:19:30.980 --> 01:19:33.210
- Thank you, that was a very nice,

01:19:33.210 --> 01:19:35.393
and that was a great example, actually,

01:19:36.330 --> 01:19:37.163
very impressed.

01:19:37.163 --> 01:19:37.996
- In your area,

01:19:37.996 --> 01:19:39.890
I'm so glad-
- I was gonna say(indistinct).

01:19:42.041 --> 01:19:44.862
Remembered one point for solar masses.

01:19:44.862 --> 01:19:46.983
That was great.

01:19:48.042 --> 01:19:51.870
So are there any other questions.

01:19:51.870 --> 01:19:55.530
If not I'd like to close
with one question myself

01:19:55.530 --> 01:19:56.480
and I think that...

01:19:58.450 --> 01:20:03.150
I wonder, when we talk about determinism

01:20:05.360 --> 01:20:08.063
and we talk about reductionism,

01:20:09.020 --> 01:20:12.610
I often have a difficulty

01:20:12.610 --> 01:20:16.470
trying to see how they sit conceptually

01:20:16.470 --> 01:20:18.030
with like the essential

01:20:18.030 --> 01:20:21.330
sort of provisional nature of science.

01:20:21.330 --> 01:20:24.100
And that I know that the provisionality,

01:20:24.100 --> 01:20:25.840
so what I'm trying to get at

01:20:25.840 --> 01:20:29.020
is the provisionality of science.

01:20:29.020 --> 01:20:33.980
What is knowable in nature
has two kinds of limits.

01:20:33.980 --> 01:20:38.200
So there may be limits that
are intrinsic to nature itself

01:20:38.200 --> 01:20:41.900
that maybe it's not
knowable beyond whatever.

01:20:41.900 --> 01:20:46.900
And the other is our own
kind of cognitive limitations

01:20:47.360 --> 01:20:50.187
and tools and capacities.

01:20:50.187 --> 01:20:55.187
So I was wondering how our
notions of reductionism

01:20:57.570 --> 01:21:00.640
and provisionality kind of,

01:21:00.640 --> 01:21:03.420
I mean do they collide or
do you see them, you know,

01:21:03.420 --> 01:21:04.780
how do you both see them?

01:21:04.780 --> 01:21:07.260
I would love to hear a little bit more

01:21:07.260 --> 01:21:09.370
about how to think about them,

01:21:09.370 --> 01:21:12.160
because these are sort of conceptually,

01:21:12.160 --> 01:21:15.313
I struggle with them
actually, I have to confess.

01:21:18.090 --> 01:21:20.830
- Where exactly do you see the connection?

01:21:20.830 --> 01:21:22.930
Why should someone's position

01:21:22.930 --> 01:21:27.930
on determinism dictate
position on reduction?

01:21:31.100 --> 01:21:36.010
As I said I think we don't
have to be reductionists.

01:21:36.010 --> 01:21:37.092
- Well, I think that because

01:21:37.092 --> 01:21:41.300
they conflict at the point of prediction

01:21:41.300 --> 01:21:44.830
about what kind of predictions

01:21:44.830 --> 01:21:49.070
therefore you can make for
future behavior of systems.

01:21:49.070 --> 01:21:51.710
So if you have a deterministic system,

01:21:51.710 --> 01:21:56.220
then you are able to predict fairly well,

01:21:56.220 --> 01:21:59.130
although limited with current limits

01:21:59.130 --> 01:22:03.510
of how much is knowable, right?

01:22:03.510 --> 01:22:04.343
- Yeah.

01:22:05.300 --> 01:22:07.580
- Reductionism is...

01:22:07.580 --> 01:22:11.310
I see the way reductionism matters

01:22:11.310 --> 01:22:16.310
is there is a way in which
you can map one system

01:22:16.660 --> 01:22:20.450
or one set of problems onto another one,

01:22:20.450 --> 01:22:23.970
which is predictable,
which was deterministic,

01:22:23.970 --> 01:22:27.040
even though this particular
one might not be.

01:22:27.040 --> 01:22:29.010
I'm trying to search
for a concrete example,

01:22:29.010 --> 01:22:33.670
but I'm not as sharp on
the fly as you are Yemima

01:22:33.670 --> 01:22:37.513
to come up with a problem that
would really illustrate this.

01:22:40.650 --> 01:22:43.546
- Well, I think it's related to models

01:22:43.546 --> 01:22:47.380
when you take one area as
a model for another area,

01:22:47.380 --> 01:22:51.030
and, as I say,

01:22:51.030 --> 01:22:56.030
determinism only applies
under very strict conditions

01:22:58.700 --> 01:23:00.593
of close systems.

01:23:05.940 --> 01:23:09.230
And even if determinism
holds in the classical world,

01:23:09.230 --> 01:23:10.410
you know there arguments

01:23:10.410 --> 01:23:11.350
that it doesn't even hold

01:23:11.350 --> 01:23:13.680
in the classical world.
- Classical world, right.

01:23:13.680 --> 01:23:16.930
- Yeah, like Newton and
airman given examples,

01:23:16.930 --> 01:23:19.640
but I think the examples are very far out

01:23:19.640 --> 01:23:21.990
and we don't have to take
them too much into account.

01:23:21.990 --> 01:23:24.940
So let's say, for us the
world is deterministic

01:23:24.940 --> 01:23:28.320
and then we learn that there
is a more fundamental level

01:23:28.320 --> 01:23:30.140
of quantum mechanics, which isn't,

01:23:30.140 --> 01:23:31.910
then, again, I think it's...

01:23:34.810 --> 01:23:38.370
Our methodological drive is to explain

01:23:38.370 --> 01:23:42.840
how what we see is compatible

01:23:42.840 --> 01:23:47.070
with what we know about
the fundamental level.

01:23:47.070 --> 01:23:50.330
And that in some cases we succeeded,

01:23:50.330 --> 01:23:51.920
in some cases we do not.

01:23:51.920 --> 01:23:53.750
You know, phase transitions.

01:23:53.750 --> 01:23:55.580
It's such a complex area

01:23:55.580 --> 01:23:57.860
we're trying to figure all
these phase transitions

01:23:57.860 --> 01:23:59.770
from what we know about
the fundamental level

01:23:59.770 --> 01:24:04.770
and we learn a lot of curious
things about analogies

01:24:04.790 --> 01:24:09.140
between different materials
that behave in similar ways

01:24:09.140 --> 01:24:12.380
although it's not the same mechanism.

01:24:12.380 --> 01:24:13.600
- [Priya] Hmm.

01:24:13.600 --> 01:24:18.120
- Magnetization is not the
same mechanism as condensation,

01:24:18.120 --> 01:24:21.870
but it's a similar mathematical structure

01:24:21.870 --> 01:24:24.450
and similar fixed points.

01:24:24.450 --> 01:24:27.660
And so it's not a reduction

01:24:27.660 --> 01:24:30.777
to the mechanisms of the
fundamental level at all

01:24:30.777 --> 01:24:32.900
and not a reduction.

01:24:32.900 --> 01:24:34.539
And determinism,

01:24:34.539 --> 01:24:38.000
I don't think I have to answer
those questions together.

01:24:38.000 --> 01:24:40.380
Determinism is a different issue

01:24:40.380 --> 01:24:41.663
from reduction.

01:24:43.900 --> 01:24:45.530
- Elise did you wanna weigh in?

01:24:45.530 --> 01:24:50.530
- Yeah, I agree with what Yemima says,

01:24:50.720 --> 01:24:52.530
but maybe from a slightly
different perspective,

01:24:52.530 --> 01:24:55.030
I mean the way I could
maybe understand reduction

01:24:55.030 --> 01:24:57.750
and determinism is the
same as that they're about

01:24:57.750 --> 01:24:59.810
establishing a particular
kind of relationship

01:24:59.810 --> 01:25:02.560
between two relata, a before and after,

01:25:02.560 --> 01:25:06.010
or cause effect relationship,
in the case of determinism

01:25:06.010 --> 01:25:09.570
or a higher order, lower
order for reduction.

01:25:09.570 --> 01:25:12.000
But my PhD thesis was all about,

01:25:12.000 --> 01:25:14.050
if this depends on a well-defined relata,

01:25:15.510 --> 01:25:18.543
then you don't get, there
are no well-defined relata,

01:25:19.950 --> 01:25:22.757
unless you're assuming
closed isolated system,.

01:25:24.350 --> 01:25:27.180
And this becomes
exacerbated at large levels

01:25:27.180 --> 01:25:30.780
and this is why you get maybe
as James Ladyman has said,

01:25:30.780 --> 01:25:34.100
like you get maybe an ontology for biology

01:25:34.100 --> 01:25:36.120
that's appropriate to that field of study

01:25:36.120 --> 01:25:41.120
and that genuinely explains and so on,

01:25:41.350 --> 01:25:44.240
but it doesn't reduce
to quantum mechanics.

01:25:44.240 --> 01:25:47.590
- It is not translatable to quantum.

01:25:47.590 --> 01:25:48.423
- Yes.

01:25:48.423 --> 01:25:49.256
- Right.

